Anyway,
so I look down,

536
00:48:08,552 --> 00:48:11,077
and there he is,
on the ground, cowering.

537
00:48:11,154 --> 00:48:14,089
- Huh?
- He's got blood on his face...

538
00:48:14,157 --> 00:48:17,183
- and he broke his fucking nose.
- Oh no.

539
00:48:17,261 --> 00:48:21,027
And he gets up and
he starts to role-play.

540
00:48:21,098 --> 00:48:22,827
- And that's when it happens.
- What?

541
00:48:22,900 --> 00:48:24,891
- He starts to cry.
- What for?

542
00:48:24,968 --> 00:48:27,835
I don't know.
What makes a man cry like that?

543
00:48:27,905 --> 00:48:29,805
Yeah, a lot of things.

544
00:48:29,873 --> 00:48:31,841
So what did you do?

545
00:48:33,877 --> 00:48:36,402
I just held him.

546
00:48:36,480 --> 00:48:38,971
I just stood there
and I held him.

547
00:48:39,049 --> 00:48:41,142
But the whole time
I was thinking,

548
00:48:41,218 --> 00:48:44,312
"You fucking weak prick,
pull yourself together."

549
00:48:44,388 --> 00:48:47,255
- Don't you want to cry sometimes?
- Yeah, but...

550
00:48:47,324 --> 00:48:49,224
- you don't, do you?
- Mmm.

551
00:48:59,403 --> 00:49:00,700
Hey.

552
00:49:00,771 --> 00:49:02,534
We ordered your food,
but we ate it.

553
00:49:03,840 --> 00:49:05,535
What's that smell?

554
00:49:07,477 --> 00:49:09,843
- Where's your mom?
- Dancing.

555
00:49:13,083 --> 00:49:15,984
- Where's your brother?
- Upstairs.

556
00:49:16,620 --> 00:49:17,552
Shit.

557
00:49:18,622 --> 00:49:19,554
Sam!

558
00:49:21,425 --> 00:49:23,052
Sam?

559
00:49:23,126 --> 00:49:25,651
Sam! Sam!

560
00:49:28,365 --> 00:49:30,731
What the fuck
is going on?

561
00:49:32,436 --> 00:49:33,994
For Christ's sake,
I'm a cop!

562
00:49:34,071 --> 00:49:38,030
- All right, you get the good stuff.
- Don't you smart-mouth me.

563
00:49:38,108 --> 00:49:40,235
- What's going on?
- Your brother is being an idiot.

564
00:49:40,310 --> 00:49:42,107
- So what's new?
- Did you know about this?

565
00:49:42,179 --> 00:49:44,204
Have you tried it?

566
00:49:44,281 --> 00:49:46,340
If you ever give
your brother that shit...

567
00:49:46,416 --> 00:49:47,974
- As if I'd give...
- Shut up!

568
00:49:48,051 --> 00:49:49,143
- No...
- Shut up!

569
00:49:49,219 --> 00:49:53,053
Give your brother this stuff, I'll
give you a thumping you won't forget.

570
00:49:53,123 --> 00:49:56,354
I don't care how big you get!
Give me the rest.

571
00:49:59,896 --> 00:50:01,124
- That's it.

572
00:50:01,198 --> 00:50:03,223
Get downstairs.

573
00:50:03,300 --> 00:50:06,292
- You're grounded, mate.
- What?

574
00:51:10,901 --> 00:51:12,596
Oh shit.

575
00:51:20,944 --> 00:51:22,605
Oh God.

576
00:52:35,585 --> 00:52:38,247
You're a very
beautiful woman, Sonja.

577
00:52:52,636 --> 00:52:54,661
I'd like
to fuck with you.

578
00:53:02,646 --> 00:53:04,614
Can I have a whiskey,
dry please?

579
00:53:10,620 --> 00:53:12,383
Excuse me.

580
00:53:19,329 --> 00:53:20,796
Hello.

581
00:53:22,098 --> 00:53:23,929
You look like
you're enjoying yourself.

582
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:25,695
Yeah, I am.

583
00:53:25,769 --> 00:53:28,738
It's good you're having fun,
while our son's at home smoking pot.

584
00:53:28,805 --> 00:53:30,067
I know.

585
00:53:30,140 --> 00:53:32,904
I told him if he's gonna do it,
he should do it at home

586
00:53:32,976 --> 00:53:36,070
- so we can control it.
- Why didn't you tell me?

587
00:53:36,146 --> 00:53:38,706
Because you haven't been
around much lately.

588
00:53:39,783 --> 00:53:41,683
I'm not having drugs
in the house.

589
00:53:41,751 --> 00:53:46,017
What are you gonna do?
Banning it won't solve the problem.

590
00:53:48,858 --> 00:53:50,883
- What are you doing here?
- What?

591
00:53:50,961 --> 00:53:52,485
What are you doing here?

592
00:53:55,265 --> 00:53:58,757
Most of the guys here
aren't much older than our son.

593
00:54:31,067 --> 00:54:34,093
- I thought we'd go back to your place.
- We can't. My mother.

594
00:54:40,010 --> 00:54:42,171
Wait. Slow down.

595
00:54:43,280 --> 00:54:45,407
Stop. Get off.

596
00:54:45,482 --> 00:54:47,143
- Jesus!

597
00:54:47,217 --> 00:54:49,276
What's wrong?

598
00:54:49,352 --> 00:54:51,217
I'm sorry.

599
00:54:51,288 --> 00:54:53,313
This was a bad idea.
Sorry.

600
00:54:56,126 --> 00:54:57,525
Fucking uptight bitch!

601
00:55:40,637 --> 00:55:42,298
Hello?

602
00:56:09,999 --> 00:56:13,901
- You found John and Valerie.
Leave a message after the tone.

603
00:56:15,038 --> 00:56:17,370
- Hi, it's me.
Are you there?

604
00:56:19,743 --> 00:56:22,644
Okay,
I've had an accident.

605
00:56:22,712 --> 00:56:24,703
I'm okay.
I can't get the car started.

606
00:56:25,882 --> 00:56:28,350
I'm on the backroad and...

607
00:56:31,054 --> 00:56:33,488
I just wanted to get home.

608
00:56:36,259 --> 00:56:38,784
I'll try your mobile. Bye.

609
00:56:42,832 --> 00:56:46,029
I called road services.
There'll be a 90-minute wait.

610
00:56:46,102 --> 00:56:50,061
Where are you?
You didn't say you'd be late.

611
00:56:50,140 --> 00:56:52,108
I can't stand this!

612
00:56:54,577 --> 00:56:56,135
Please...

613
00:56:58,114 --> 00:57:00,014
Please, I need you.

614
00:57:34,751 --> 00:57:37,083
John?

615
00:57:41,791 --> 00:57:43,486
There is a man.

616
00:57:45,562 --> 00:57:46,790
Patrick.

617
00:57:50,200 --> 00:57:52,327
He's a client and he's...

618
00:57:56,072 --> 00:57:57,699
he's gay.

619
00:58:09,052 --> 00:58:12,419
I don't understand this.
I don't understand...

620
00:58:13,490 --> 00:58:14,957
us...

621
00:58:16,659 --> 00:58:18,627
anymore.

622
00:58:24,100 --> 00:58:27,365
I don't want this
to be happening to us.

623
00:58:37,847 --> 00:58:38,973
Oh...

624
00:58:39,048 --> 00:58:40,845
There are lights.

625
00:58:40,917 --> 00:58:43,715
There's a car coming.
I'll wave it down.

626
00:58:45,221 --> 00:58:49,021
Wait for me.
We'll talk when I get home, okay?

627
00:58:49,092 --> 00:58:51,083
Bye.

628
00:58:51,160 --> 00:58:53,185
I love you.

629
01:00:22,552 --> 01:00:24,679
- You need sleep.
- You wish.

630
01:00:24,754 --> 01:00:29,350
- What have we got?
- Locals got a call, about 12:30 AM

631
01:00:29,425 --> 01:00:32,519
from the husband. He gets home late,
his wife's not there.

632
01:00:32,595 --> 01:00:35,428
She's left messages on the answering
machine, saying she ran off the road,

633
01:00:35,498 --> 01:00:38,990
she's making a call from a phone box,
about 2kms down the road.

634
01:00:39,068 --> 01:00:42,333
Last call says she saw a car coming,
she's gonna wave it down.

635
01:00:42,405 --> 01:00:44,270
But she never makes it.

636
01:00:44,340 --> 01:00:46,535
$50 says
it's the husband.

637
01:00:46,609 --> 01:00:48,406
You're on.

638
01:00:55,218 --> 01:00:56,583
Mr. Somers?

639
01:00:56,653 --> 01:00:59,781
Knox. My wife's
name's Somers.

640
01:01:01,057 --> 01:01:02,888
I'm Detective Zat.

641
01:01:02,959 --> 01:01:05,393
This is my colleague,
Detective Weis.

642
01:01:07,230 --> 01:01:09,858
We've located
your wife's car, Mr. Knox.

643
01:01:12,001 --> 01:01:13,798
Do you mind if we come in?

644
01:01:23,913 --> 01:01:27,542
Mr. Knox, it appears that
your wife ran off the road.

645
01:01:28,618 --> 01:01:31,451
There's a telephone box
several kilometers further along.

646
01:01:32,989 --> 01:01:37,221
- Should I go there?
- We're conducting a search, but...

647
01:01:37,293 --> 01:01:41,753
if she accepted a lift from somebody,
it's unlikely she'll be there.

648
01:01:41,831 --> 01:01:43,628
Would you mind answering
a few questions?

649
01:01:43,700 --> 01:01:45,964
I've been through all this
with the police.

650
01:01:46,035 --> 01:01:49,766
I know, but would you mind telling me
what happened last night?

651
01:01:51,474 --> 01:01:53,704
I got home around midnight.

652
01:01:53,776 --> 01:01:55,937
Her car wasn't here.

653
01:01:56,012 --> 01:01:57,980
I came in,
I checked the machine.

654
01:01:58,047 --> 01:02:00,277
There were
a couple of calls.

655
01:02:00,349 --> 01:02:02,977
The last message said
there was a car coming

656
01:02:03,052 --> 01:02:05,111
and she was going
to wave it down.

657
01:02:05,188 --> 01:02:08,555
- That's when you called the police?
- No, I waited about 20 minutes.

658
01:02:08,624 --> 01:02:12,287
- That's how long it would have...
- So you called at about 12:20?

659
01:02:12,361 --> 01:02:14,022
Yes, more or less.

660
01:02:14,097 --> 01:02:17,123
Do you have a photo of your wife
we could have, please?

661
01:02:27,710 --> 01:02:28,972
Thank you.

662
01:02:33,716 --> 01:02:35,684
How was your wife
yesterday?

663
01:02:36,753 --> 01:02:38,345
- Fine.
- Nothing troubling her?

664
01:02:38,421 --> 01:02:39,353
No.

665
01:02:41,224 --> 01:02:45,183
I am trying to find out
about your wife's emotional state.

666
01:02:45,261 --> 01:02:49,357
Right now, I'd say
it's pretty bad, wouldn't you?

667
01:02:49,432 --> 01:02:51,195
None of this
is particularly pleasant.

668
01:02:51,267 --> 01:02:55,328
- I can imagine.
- Imagine what? You're married?

669
01:02:55,404 --> 01:02:57,201
Yeah.

670
01:02:57,273 --> 01:02:59,298
If your wife got
into a stranger's car...

671
01:02:59,375 --> 01:03:02,367
a man, let's assume...
and didn't come home,

672
01:03:02,445 --> 01:03:04,208
what would you imagine?

673
01:03:07,583 --> 01:03:09,574
Right now,
I'd be going mad.

674
01:03:11,420 --> 01:03:12,717
Yeah.

675
01:03:12,789 --> 01:03:14,552
Mr. Knox,
we need the tape.

676
01:03:27,069 --> 01:03:29,128
She...
this is private.

677
01:03:30,206 --> 01:03:33,107
- In what sense?
- She's upset.

678
01:03:34,177 --> 01:03:37,010
She wasn't expecting anyone
to listen to it.

679
01:03:38,714 --> 01:03:41,308
I'll make sure
this is returned to you.

680
01:03:54,430 --> 01:03:58,196
- You didn't wake me up last night.
- I got in late.

681
01:03:58,267 --> 01:04:00,394
What's with the face?

682
01:04:00,469 --> 01:04:02,994
- I fell over.
- You were pissed?

683
01:04:03,072 --> 01:04:04,198
A little.

684
01:04:05,875 --> 01:04:07,240
Come on, kids.

685
01:04:07,310 --> 01:04:09,141
You packed your bag, Hannah?

686
01:04:36,172 --> 01:04:38,470
- Quickly. Come on.
- Hi!

687
01:04:38,541 --> 01:04:40,372
- Hi.
- Hi.

688
01:04:42,578 --> 01:04:44,205
Seatbelts on, quickly.

689
01:04:46,015 --> 01:04:50,645
- Nik got in late last night.
- Got nothing better to do than spying?

690
01:04:50,720 --> 01:04:51,778
- What?

691
01:04:54,257 --> 01:04:56,919
- What?
- You know,

692
01:04:56,993 --> 01:05:00,929
don't invite Nik in for coffee
when I'm not here.

693
01:05:00,963 --> 01:05:01,861
All right?

694
01:05:01,931 --> 01:05:04,559
Paula?! Hey.

695
01:05:12,541 --> 01:05:14,338
That's
the appointment book.

696
01:05:14,410 --> 01:05:17,504
All her notes and session tapes
are kept in a filing cabinet.

697
01:05:17,580 --> 01:05:19,639
- Do you mind?
- No.

698
01:05:22,218 --> 01:05:25,483
- How was she yesterday?
- All right.

699
01:05:25,554 --> 01:05:29,081
Is she the kind of person
that would get into a stranger's car?

700
01:05:29,158 --> 01:05:30,557
No.

701
01:05:30,626 --> 01:05:32,594
Not after what happened
to her daughter.

702
01:05:34,063 --> 01:05:38,523
Sarah, I'd like you to print me
a list of her current clients,

703
01:05:38,601 --> 01:05:41,934
- addresses and phone numbers too.
- Is that ethical?

704
01:05:43,072 --> 01:05:44,664
Probably not.

705
01:08:50,759 --> 01:08:54,217
- It's not that he might have...

706
01:08:55,297 --> 01:08:57,993
slept with
another woman...

707
01:08:59,635 --> 01:09:02,661
it's that
he might not tell me.

708
01:09:03,739 --> 01:09:05,798
That would be
the betrayal.

709
01:09:09,945 --> 01:09:11,970
-
Do you still love him?

710
01:09:27,396 --> 01:09:30,957
Good evening.
Richard Morecroft with ABC News.

711
01:09:31,033 --> 01:09:32,967
The police are inquiring

712
01:09:33,035 --> 01:09:36,801
into the disappearance of a woman
in Bushland, north of the city.

713
01:09:36,872 --> 01:09:41,172
Psychiatrist Valerie Somers
was last seen on Friday night.

714
01:09:41,243 --> 01:09:45,077
Her car was found abandoned
along the Lower Ridge Road.

715
01:09:45,147 --> 01:09:48,878
She might have accepted a lift
from a passing motorist.

716
01:09:48,951 --> 01:09:51,613
Ms. Somers has recently
completed a book

717
01:09:51,687 --> 01:09:53,780
about the murder
of her own daughter.

718
01:09:53,856 --> 01:09:56,518
The body of 11-year-old
Eleanor Knox

719
01:09:56,592 --> 01:09:59,959
was found dumped in a city
laneway 18 months ago.

720
01:10:00,029 --> 01:10:02,657
Police are appealing
to the public for information

721
01:10:02,731 --> 01:10:05,359
regarding
Ms. Somers' disappearance.

722
01:11:36,025 --> 01:11:38,619
Why do you think
she turned off the freeway?

723
01:11:38,694 --> 01:11:40,958
Some people say
it's shorter.

724
01:11:41,930 --> 01:11:43,329
Who's Patrick?

725
01:11:45,167 --> 01:11:46,725
I don't know.

726
01:11:48,070 --> 01:11:51,130
She mentioned she was having
some trouble with a client.

727
01:11:51,206 --> 01:11:53,037
What kind of trouble?

728
01:11:53,108 --> 01:11:56,009
She didn't go into it.
She doesn't talk about her clients.

729
01:11:56,078 --> 01:11:58,308
- Why not?
- It's unprofessional.

730
01:11:58,380 --> 01:12:01,144
- Even between husband and wife?
- Yes.

731
01:12:03,752 --> 01:12:06,619
- I tell my wife everything.
- That surprises me.

732
01:12:06,689 --> 01:12:08,020
Why?

733
01:12:08,090 --> 01:12:10,388
Most men hold
something back.

734
01:12:15,864 --> 01:12:18,355
You're some kind
of academic, aren't you?

735
01:12:18,434 --> 01:12:20,265
I'm Dean of Law.

736
01:12:20,336 --> 01:12:23,237
I studied at Harvard.
That's where Valerie and I met.

737
01:12:25,074 --> 01:12:28,874
I don't understand why she'd get
into a car with a stranger.

738
01:12:29,945 --> 01:12:32,880
Maybe she didn't.

739
01:12:32,948 --> 01:12:35,007
Maybe she knew him.

740
01:12:38,220 --> 01:12:41,519
- How's your marriage been lately?
- Fine. How's yours?

741
01:12:41,590 --> 01:12:43,649
Up and down.
Where were you Friday night?

742
01:12:43,726 --> 01:12:45,751
Am I a suspect in
my wife's disappearance?

743
01:12:45,828 --> 01:12:47,796
Where were you
Friday night?

744
01:12:47,863 --> 01:12:49,797
I was at work.

745
01:12:49,865 --> 01:12:52,026
Can anybody verify that?

746
01:12:52,101 --> 01:12:54,399
No, I was alone.

747
01:12:54,470 --> 01:12:56,563
Nobody saw me.

748
01:13:00,509 --> 01:13:04,240
Nine times out of 10
when a wife goes missing,

749
01:13:04,313 --> 01:13:07,009
the husband knows
something about it.

750
01:13:08,083 --> 01:13:09,744
You're a prick.

751
01:13:12,454 --> 01:13:15,321
The young constable
will give you a ride.

752
01:13:20,229 --> 01:13:22,697
- Anyway, we've been

753
01:13:22,765 --> 01:13:24,392
seeing each other
for a while.

754
01:13:24,466 --> 01:13:26,229
-
And you like him?

755
01:13:27,035 --> 01:13:28,696
- Yes, I do.

756
01:13:29,905 --> 01:13:31,736
Very much.

757
01:13:31,807 --> 01:13:33,172
- So?

758
01:13:34,643 --> 01:13:36,634
-
He comes encumbered...

759
01:13:36,712 --> 01:13:38,942
with a wife.

760
01:13:52,561 --> 01:13:56,759
- Don't you have a home to go to?
- Yes. Do you?

761
01:13:57,833 --> 01:13:59,528
Did you find anything?

762
01:13:59,601 --> 01:14:02,001
She dedicated
the book to John.

763
01:14:02,070 --> 01:14:04,061
"For teaching me
to trust again."

764
01:14:05,140 --> 01:14:07,267
- Did you listen to Phelan's tapes?
- Yeah.

765
01:14:07,342 --> 01:14:09,970
- What did you think?
- She didn't like the man.

766
01:14:13,849 --> 01:14:15,874
Go home.
You got an early start.

767
01:14:15,951 --> 01:14:18,977
- What about you?
- Soon.

768
01:14:19,054 --> 01:14:20,146
Okay.

769
01:14:26,829 --> 01:14:29,127
You really look like shit.
Go home.

770
01:14:30,199 --> 01:14:31,530
Thank you.

771
01:14:31,600 --> 01:14:33,761
Talked to mystery man yet?

772
01:14:35,204 --> 01:14:37,035
He never came back.

773
01:14:38,941 --> 01:14:40,533
Silly bugger.

774
01:14:54,389 --> 01:14:56,414
I'm not asleep.

775
01:14:59,895 --> 01:15:01,726
Did you watch the news?

776
01:15:02,831 --> 01:15:04,423
Yeah.

777
01:15:05,801 --> 01:15:07,200
Will you find her?

778
01:15:09,037 --> 01:15:10,732
It's not looking good.

779
01:15:15,511 --> 01:15:17,911
I saw her client list,
Sonja.

780
01:15:20,148 --> 01:15:21,877
Why didn't you tell me?

781
01:15:28,123 --> 01:15:31,183
Because it was private.

782
01:15:33,896 --> 01:15:36,456
It was just something
I had to do.

783
01:15:39,835 --> 01:15:42,998
There was a time when there was
no private between you and me.

784
01:16:06,128 --> 01:16:09,097
That is because I had somebody
I could talk to.

785
01:16:09,164 --> 01:16:11,291
- I have to tell you something...
- I have to tell you...

786
01:16:11,366 --> 01:16:13,197
I had an affair.

787
01:16:20,776 --> 01:16:23,074
I slept with her twice.

788
01:16:27,316 --> 01:16:30,479
I know it hurts you.

789
01:16:30,552 --> 01:16:32,179
It hurts her...

790
01:16:37,159 --> 01:16:38,592
Why?

791
01:16:41,697 --> 01:16:43,324
Because I'm numb.

792
01:16:46,435 --> 01:16:48,767
I can't feel
anything anymore.

793
01:16:52,774 --> 01:16:54,833
Just totally
fucking numb.

794
01:17:09,458 --> 01:17:11,289
Why did you sleep
on the couch?

795
01:17:11,360 --> 01:17:14,955
I came in late last night.
I didn't want to wake your mama.

796
01:17:17,065 --> 01:17:18,532
Are you fighting?

797
01:17:20,469 --> 01:17:23,529
- Yeah, a bit.
- Why?

798
01:17:24,606 --> 01:17:27,234
There's something
we've got to sort out.

799
01:17:27,309 --> 01:17:30,039
- You all right, Mom?
- Yeah.

800
01:17:32,681 --> 01:17:34,239
I'll be in the car.

801
01:17:36,785 --> 01:17:40,243
Can you grab something to eat?
We're running late.

802
01:17:47,295 --> 01:17:49,627
Are we gonna
talk about this?

803
01:17:49,698 --> 01:17:53,134
Or you just going to punish me?
This is how you're gonna punish me?

804
01:17:54,469 --> 01:17:55,959
I fucked up.

805
01:17:56,038 --> 01:17:58,836
- People fuck up.
- Really? I don't.

806
01:17:58,907 --> 01:18:03,003
You know what's so easy?
It's easy to go and find somebody.

807
01:18:03,078 --> 01:18:07,344
You know what's hard?
What's hard is not to.

808
01:18:07,416 --> 01:18:09,407
Sonja, listen.
I just want...

809
01:18:09,484 --> 01:18:11,315
Get off me.

810
01:18:11,386 --> 01:18:13,320
God.

811
01:18:13,388 --> 01:18:16,721
We'll talk about this
tonight, all right?

812
01:18:16,792 --> 01:18:19,124
Oh... get fucked!

813
01:18:19,194 --> 01:18:21,628
I don't even know
if I'll be here later.

814
01:18:32,607 --> 01:18:33,869
Hi.

815
01:18:35,210 --> 01:18:36,939
Did you know?

816
01:19:00,235 --> 01:19:01,259
You're ready?

817
01:19:57,659 --> 01:19:59,092
Pete?

818
01:19:59,161 --> 01:20:00,856
It's me.

819
01:20:02,564 --> 01:20:04,589
Can you come over?

820
01:20:16,077 --> 01:20:18,739
- What number is it?
- 406.

821
01:20:26,688 --> 01:20:28,485
You sure
you're up to this?

822
01:20:32,594 --> 01:20:33,993
Mr. Phelan.

823
01:20:34,062 --> 01:20:36,826
We're investigating the disappearance
of Valerie Somers.

824
01:20:36,898 --> 01:20:38,889
We were hoping
you could help us.

825
01:20:41,203 --> 01:20:44,036
It's not a good time.

826
01:20:45,106 --> 01:20:47,336
- I was out late.
- Who with?

827
01:20:48,610 --> 01:20:51,511
Mr. Phelan,
the woman's missing.

828
01:21:02,958 --> 01:21:05,950
- You know what's happened to her?
- Not yet.

829
01:21:06,027 --> 01:21:09,258
You had an appointment with her?
Can you tell us how she was?

830
01:21:11,132 --> 01:21:14,260
She seemed all right.
I don't know.

831
01:21:14,336 --> 01:21:15,860
You don't know?

832
01:21:15,937 --> 01:21:20,203
She's the therapist.
I wasn't focused on how she was.

833
01:21:20,275 --> 01:21:21,936
How do you
get along with her?

834
01:21:22,010 --> 01:21:24,672
- Fine.
- That's it?

835
01:21:24,746 --> 01:21:26,179
Fine?

836
01:21:29,150 --> 01:21:31,812
We didn't end our last session
on very good terms.

837
01:21:31,887 --> 01:21:33,752
-
Why is that?

838
01:21:33,822 --> 01:21:36,382
- We disagreed about something.
- What was that?

839
01:21:36,458 --> 01:21:39,427
What? That guy
you've been fucking?

840
01:21:39,494 --> 01:21:42,088
- Married guy?
- How did you know about that?

841
01:21:42,163 --> 01:21:44,563
- She records all her sessions.
- That's private...

842
01:21:44,633 --> 01:21:48,125
- Yes, but under the circumstances...
- That's my life!

843
01:21:51,106 --> 01:21:52,835
Is there somebody
in that room?

844
01:21:52,908 --> 01:21:55,138
Who is it?
Your boyfriend?

845
01:21:55,210 --> 01:21:58,668
- Could you ask him to come out?
- He has nothing...

846
01:21:58,747 --> 01:21:59,941
- Leon!
- What's the matter with you?

847
01:22:00,015 --> 01:22:01,915
- You don't have the right...
- Who are you?!

848
01:22:01,983 --> 01:22:04,076
You have
no fucking right!

849
01:22:12,794 --> 01:22:14,227
Finished?

850
01:22:22,737 --> 01:22:24,398
That went well.

851
01:22:24,472 --> 01:22:26,963
Your marriage is falling apart
and so are you.

852
01:22:27,042 --> 01:22:30,876
- It's none of your business.
- It is if you can't do your job!

853
01:22:30,946 --> 01:22:33,312
If you don't like the way
I'm handling things,

854
01:22:33,381 --> 01:22:35,372
take it up at the station.

855
01:22:35,450 --> 01:22:37,384
Push.

856
01:23:33,441 --> 01:23:34,999
- Hello?
- Dylan?

857
01:23:35,076 --> 01:23:36,008
Hi, Dad.

858
01:23:38,113 --> 01:23:40,240
Could I speak to your mom?

859
01:23:43,018 --> 01:23:45,316
No, she's still
pissed off at you.

860
01:23:47,522 --> 01:23:49,217
All right.

861
01:23:49,290 --> 01:23:51,281
Tell her...

862
01:23:52,360 --> 01:23:55,295
- tell her I'll be home soon.
- All right. See you, Dad.

863
01:23:57,699 --> 01:23:59,189
What did he say?

864
01:24:00,835 --> 01:24:04,236
He said that he's sorry,
that he loves you,

865
01:24:04,305 --> 01:24:07,035
and he wants you to stop
being angry with him.

866
01:24:34,235 --> 01:24:36,465
You look bereft, Leon.

867
01:24:36,538 --> 01:24:38,563
The other question is,
why don't you?

868
01:24:41,076 --> 01:24:43,476
Don't be deceived
by appearances.

869
01:24:43,545 --> 01:24:45,410
Want a whiskey?

870
01:24:51,653 --> 01:24:54,121
- Somebody
may have hurt your wife.

871
01:24:54,189 --> 01:24:57,556
- I need to know if it was you.
- I didn't hurt her.

872
01:24:57,625 --> 01:24:59,855
- She was upset on the phone.
- She was afraid.

873
01:24:59,928 --> 01:25:01,919
- Of what?
- Of being alone.

874
01:25:01,996 --> 01:25:04,692
Of me not being
there for her.

875
01:25:04,766 --> 01:25:06,393
Why weren't you
there for her?

876
01:25:10,605 --> 01:25:13,540
While your wife
was in some phone box,

877
01:25:13,608 --> 01:25:17,374
calling for your help,
where were you?

878
01:25:18,746 --> 01:25:20,771
Are you seeing someone else?

879
01:25:20,849 --> 01:25:22,874
- Is it an affair?
- No.

880
01:25:22,951 --> 01:25:24,885
With a man?
Is that what's going on?

881
01:25:24,953 --> 01:25:28,514
I believe that's what
Valerie thought was going on.

882
01:25:28,590 --> 01:25:30,217
What are you
talking about?

883
01:25:30,291 --> 01:25:34,227
For some reason, she believe
you were involved with Patrick Phelan.

884
01:25:34,295 --> 01:25:37,628
Is that it?
Were you seeing men on the side?

885
01:25:37,699 --> 01:25:39,792
- I don't have to listen to this?
- Yes, you do.

886
01:25:39,868 --> 01:25:42,268
My wife's out there somewhere.
What are you doing about it?

887
01:25:42,337 --> 01:25:44,237
I'm trying to find her.

888
01:25:44,305 --> 01:25:46,671
But I need to know
what's inside her head.

889
01:25:46,741 --> 01:25:48,538
I don't know.

890
01:25:51,679 --> 01:25:53,442
I don't know.

891
01:25:59,621 --> 01:26:01,714
Have you ever
cheated on your wife?

892
01:26:05,760 --> 01:26:06,988
No.

893
01:26:07,061 --> 01:26:10,258
- Never desired another woman?
- Yes, of course.

894
01:26:10,331 --> 01:26:11,889
- But you never acted on it?
- No.

895
01:26:11,966 --> 01:26:14,366
Well, you're
a better man than I am.

896
01:26:15,436 --> 01:26:17,063
So there is someone else?

897
01:26:17,138 --> 01:26:18,935
No.

898
01:26:20,441 --> 01:26:22,705
There was someone once.

899
01:26:22,777 --> 01:26:24,301
A woman.

900
01:26:25,613 --> 01:26:29,140
Once that's happened, you're never
entirely believed again.

901
01:26:29,217 --> 01:26:31,242
Something gets broken,

902
01:26:31,319 --> 01:26:33,879
permanently.
Trust, I suppose.

903
01:26:33,955 --> 01:26:36,924
When that happens,
anything's possible, it would seem.

904
01:26:40,628 --> 01:26:44,325
You don't lose a daughter,
like we lost Eleanor,

905
01:26:45,400 --> 01:26:47,334
without some damage.

906
01:26:49,404 --> 01:26:51,304
So where were you?

907
01:26:54,576 --> 01:26:56,703
I left work late.

908
01:26:58,913 --> 01:27:02,815
I stopped at the place
where my daughter was killed.

909
01:27:02,884 --> 01:27:05,819
I go there... a lot.

910
01:27:07,655 --> 01:27:11,591
- Valerie didn't know that.
- You didn't tell her?

911
01:27:13,261 --> 01:27:15,092
Why not, John?

912
01:27:23,471 --> 01:27:25,962
What holds
your marriage together, Leon?

913
01:27:34,148 --> 01:27:35,445
Loyalty?

914
01:27:36,517 --> 01:27:37,484
Love?

915
01:27:39,454 --> 01:27:42,446
Maybe habits sometimes,
passion, our kids.

916
01:27:46,127 --> 01:27:48,652
Ours was held together
by grief.

917
01:27:50,665 --> 01:27:53,327
There wasn't
much else left.

918
01:27:54,402 --> 01:27:56,165
You didn't love her
anymore?

919
01:27:56,237 --> 01:28:00,936
I'm saying that sometimes,
love isn't enough.

920
01:28:11,352 --> 01:28:12,683
- Leon!

921
01:28:12,754 --> 01:28:14,187
Where the hell
have you been?

922
01:28:14,255 --> 01:28:17,520
We got a call from a man,
saying his wife saw a neighbor

923
01:28:17,592 --> 01:28:21,028
throw a shoe into a vacant lot
on the night Valerie disappeared.

924
01:28:21,095 --> 01:28:23,427
She's got the shoe.
Black leather.

925
01:28:23,498 --> 01:28:25,466
Where are we going?

926
01:28:34,542 --> 01:28:37,170
- This could be tricky.
- Why?

927
01:28:38,813 --> 01:28:40,542
I know the woman.

928
01:28:40,615 --> 01:28:42,310
Oh Jesus!

929
01:28:53,027 --> 01:28:55,825
- Detective Claudia Weis.
- Leon!

930
01:28:56,898 --> 01:28:59,594
- We had a drink the other night.
- How are you?

931
01:28:59,667 --> 01:29:00,634
Good.

932
01:29:00,702 --> 01:29:02,863
You'd better come in.
My wife's pretty upset.

933
01:29:09,711 --> 01:29:11,941
- Jane, it's the police.

934
01:29:12,013 --> 01:29:14,777
- This is Leon and...
- Claudia.

935
01:29:14,849 --> 01:29:16,714
- And Claudia. Jane.
- Is that the shoe?

936
01:29:16,784 --> 01:29:18,752
Yeah.

937
01:29:19,887 --> 01:29:22,754
You shouldn't have touched the shoe,

938
01:29:22,824 --> 01:29:24,519
- Mrs...?
- O'May.

939
01:29:24,592 --> 01:29:26,583
It's Jane O'May.

940
01:29:26,661 --> 01:29:28,720
Right, Mrs. O'May,
you shouldn't have touched it.

941
01:29:29,797 --> 01:29:30,991
Well, I did.

942
01:29:32,133 --> 01:29:34,727
Yeah, but you shouldn't have.

943
01:29:34,802 --> 01:29:37,293
Well, I did, didn't I?

944
01:29:37,372 --> 01:29:39,033
It's on the table.

945
01:29:40,108 --> 01:29:42,770
- Could we have some coffee?
- Yeah.

946
01:29:42,844 --> 01:29:44,641
It's out
the back here. Thanks.

947
01:29:44,712 --> 01:29:46,612
I'll give you a hand.

948
01:30:03,197 --> 01:30:04,858
Are you all right?

949
01:30:08,336 --> 01:30:11,601
- Have you got a light?
- Yeah.

950
01:30:16,644 --> 01:30:18,441
How do you want to handle this?

951
01:30:21,182 --> 01:30:23,082
You're a policeman, aren't you?

952
01:30:23,151 --> 01:30:25,381
Why don't you just do your job?

953
01:30:26,788 --> 01:30:28,619
I've never seen you before.

954
01:30:34,362 --> 01:30:36,660
-
Can I speak to Paula, please?

955
01:30:38,733 --> 01:30:40,257
- It's urgent.

956
01:30:40,334 --> 01:30:43,098
Can you tell her to
call me as soon as she can?

957
01:30:43,171 --> 01:30:45,230
Yes, as soon as she can, please.

958
01:30:51,045 --> 01:30:52,945
Leave it!
Go get your brother.

959
01:30:58,986 --> 01:31:01,978
Nik D'Amato? Detective
Claudia Weis, City Central.

960
01:31:02,056 --> 01:31:05,457
My kids. I need
someone to watch my kids.

961
01:31:07,895 --> 01:31:10,420
Right. I'll give you
a couple of minutes.

962
01:31:17,205 --> 01:31:19,503
- So I go to the window,

963
01:31:19,574 --> 01:31:21,201
at about 11:30.

964
01:31:21,275 --> 01:31:23,800
I go to the window,
and he's chucking that.

965
01:31:23,878 --> 01:31:26,108
And he threw it over there,

966
01:31:26,180 --> 01:31:28,512
and he was looking
like he was...

967
01:31:28,583 --> 01:31:30,710
really guilty.

968
01:31:52,039 --> 01:31:54,030
Nik.

969
01:31:54,108 --> 01:31:55,837
- You're back, Pete?

970
01:31:57,044 --> 01:31:58,773
Only sort of.

971
01:32:00,014 --> 01:32:03,211
- How are you?
- Good. And you?

972
01:32:04,285 --> 01:32:05,946
I'm in a bit of trouble.

973
01:32:07,021 --> 01:32:09,649
Can you take the kids?

974
01:32:09,724 --> 01:32:11,316
Just till Paula gets back.

975
01:32:13,895 --> 01:32:16,557
- I wouldn't ask
unless I really needed help.

976
01:32:22,503 --> 01:32:24,903
We'll take them.

977
01:32:24,972 --> 01:32:26,769
Thanks.

978
01:32:26,841 --> 01:32:28,741
Here you go.

979
01:32:29,911 --> 01:32:31,276
- Thanks.

980
01:32:32,346 --> 01:32:36,180
There's pajamas, toothbrush...

981
01:32:36,250 --> 01:32:39,185
there's a video and some
other stuff in there as well.

982
01:32:40,321 --> 01:32:41,879
Thanks very much, okay?

983
01:32:41,956 --> 01:32:43,787
It's time to go.

984
01:32:43,858 --> 01:32:46,656
No, Daddy, don't go.
Don't go!

985
01:32:46,727 --> 01:32:49,491
Come on.
I'll be back soon.

986
01:32:49,564 --> 01:32:52,226
- Come on.
- No! No!

987
01:32:57,505 --> 01:33:00,167
How did you get the
scratches on your face?

988
01:33:02,476 --> 01:33:05,502
- I want to see my wife.
- She's on her way.

989
01:33:09,116 --> 01:33:11,676
Can you tell us where
you were Friday night?

990
01:33:12,753 --> 01:33:14,482
I want to see Paula.

991
01:33:14,555 --> 01:33:16,921
You are in deep shit, mate.

992
01:33:16,991 --> 01:33:18,788
Your wife can't help you.

993
01:33:20,094 --> 01:33:22,619
- Do I know you?
- I doubt it.

994
01:33:23,998 --> 01:33:26,762
- I've seen you before.
- Shut up! Shut up!

995
01:33:33,007 --> 01:33:35,908
- You were next door at Jane's place.
- I told you to shut up!

996
01:33:45,052 --> 01:33:46,917
Where are my kids?

997
01:33:46,988 --> 01:33:49,582
- Where are my bloody kids?!
- With your neighbor.

998
01:33:49,657 --> 01:33:51,420
- Who are you?
- Calm down.

999
01:33:51,492 --> 01:33:54,928
- I don't want to be calm.
- Can I get you something?

1000
01:33:54,996 --> 01:33:57,021
Yes, you can get
me my husband.

1001
01:33:57,098 --> 01:33:59,931
- And get me out of here!
- Can you just step in here?

1002
01:34:08,643 --> 01:34:10,508
Mrs. D'Amato.

1003
01:34:10,578 --> 01:34:13,809
I'm Detective Sergeant Zat.

1004
01:34:13,881 --> 01:34:16,714
I believe you met
Detective Constable Weis.

1005
01:34:17,818 --> 01:34:19,445
I want to see Nik.

1006
01:34:20,521 --> 01:34:22,819
Your husband is helping us
with our inquiries.

1007
01:34:22,890 --> 01:34:24,721
Bullshit.

1008
01:34:26,460 --> 01:34:29,486
He was seen throwing a shoe
into a vacant lot.

1009
01:34:31,298 --> 01:34:32,925
Who saw him?

1010
01:34:33,000 --> 01:34:37,334
A search was conducted
in the block opposite your house.

1011
01:34:38,572 --> 01:34:39,698
Mmm?

1012
01:34:39,774 --> 01:34:41,207
Another one?

1013
01:34:41,275 --> 01:34:44,802
My kids play there.
Every kid on the street plays there.

1014
01:34:45,880 --> 01:34:47,711
They found the shoe.

1015
01:34:47,782 --> 01:34:50,979
It was identified as belonging
to Ms. Valerie Somers.

1016
01:34:51,052 --> 01:34:53,782
She's been missing
since last Friday night.

1017
01:35:01,729 --> 01:35:03,526
Paula!

1018
01:35:10,805 --> 01:35:14,764
- Hello?
- Janey, it's Paula.

1019
01:35:14,842 --> 01:35:16,309
Hi.

1020
01:35:17,712 --> 01:35:19,339
- Is Andrew awake?

1021
01:35:19,413 --> 01:35:21,677
Your kids are fine.

1022
01:35:21,749 --> 01:35:24,912
- You know?
- Maybe I could talk to Hannah.

1023
01:35:24,985 --> 01:35:27,954
- No, she's asleep.

1024
01:35:28,022 --> 01:35:32,118
- The baby?
- You know what? They're all asleep.

1025
01:35:33,527 --> 01:35:35,620
Sorry about this, Janey.

1026
01:35:37,364 --> 01:35:39,559
Nik's in trouble.

1027
01:35:39,633 --> 01:35:42,830
They won't let me see him.
I don't know what to do.

1028
01:35:42,903 --> 01:35:45,963
You know what?
It's okay.

1029
01:35:46,040 --> 01:35:47,667
Everything's okay.

1030
01:35:47,742 --> 01:35:49,573
- Your kids are really safe.

1031
01:35:49,643 --> 01:35:51,634
I'm sorry.

1032
01:35:54,648 --> 01:35:56,843
I'll get there as soon as I can.

1033
01:35:56,917 --> 01:35:59,818
- Okay.
- Thank you.

1034
01:35:59,887 --> 01:36:01,548
Bye, Janey.

1035
01:36:07,428 --> 01:36:09,589
Does she know
you rang the police?

1036
01:36:10,731 --> 01:36:11,823
No.

1037
01:36:35,256 --> 01:36:37,121
They say you've...

1038
01:36:38,192 --> 01:36:40,217
hurt some woman, Nik.

1039
01:36:51,505 --> 01:36:53,097
I didn't, babe.

1040
01:36:55,476 --> 01:36:56,943
I didn't touch her.

1041
01:37:44,792 --> 01:37:47,625
Don't. Not yet.

1042
01:37:51,432 --> 01:37:54,230
- What is it, Hannah?
- The baby's sick.

1043
01:37:58,706 --> 01:38:00,970
What is it?

1044
01:38:01,041 --> 01:38:02,508
What is it?

1045
01:38:04,178 --> 01:38:05,975
He's burning up.

1046
01:38:06,046 --> 01:38:09,447
- Get us a flannel. A wet one.
- Panadol.

1047
01:38:09,516 --> 01:38:11,848
- What?
- He needs Panadol.

1048
01:38:11,919 --> 01:38:13,181
Panadol.

1049
01:38:14,922 --> 01:38:17,618
- Poor little thing.
- It's all right for babies?

1050
01:38:17,691 --> 01:38:20,922
- I don't know. Only get half.
- Baby Panadol.

1051
01:38:20,995 --> 01:38:23,020
- What?
- Baby Panadol.

1052
01:38:23,097 --> 01:38:27,090
- You'll have to go to the chemist's.
- There's some at our house.

1053
01:38:51,725 --> 01:38:53,920
I'd met some mates for a drink.

1054
01:38:53,994 --> 01:38:57,589
We used to work together.
It's something we keep up.

1055
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:03,492
We drank more than we should have,
so I took the backroad.

1056
01:39:04,571 --> 01:39:07,062
The police don't patrol it.

1057
01:39:09,410 --> 01:39:11,708
It must have been about...

1058
01:39:11,779 --> 01:39:13,679
a quarter to 12:00...

1059
01:39:15,516 --> 01:39:18,917
and I see this woman standing
at the side of the road.

1060
01:39:18,986 --> 01:39:20,977
I don't want to stop.

1061
01:39:21,055 --> 01:39:25,014
It's late, and I'm thinking
Paula will get worried.

1062
01:39:25,092 --> 01:39:27,822
But what do I do?
The woman needs help.

1063
01:39:27,895 --> 01:39:29,089
So I pull over.

1064
01:39:31,231 --> 01:39:33,222
My car ran off the road.

1065
01:39:35,436 --> 01:39:36,460
Get in.

1066
01:39:44,411 --> 01:39:45,969
Thanks.

1067
01:39:52,152 --> 01:39:53,813
What's your name?

1068
01:39:55,522 --> 01:39:56,580
Valerie.

1069
01:39:56,657 --> 01:39:58,352
I'm Nik.

1070
01:40:01,795 --> 01:40:05,196
- It turns out she lives
in one of those houses by the Bay.

1071
01:40:05,265 --> 01:40:07,756
There's a string
of houses along there.

1072
01:40:07,835 --> 01:40:11,066
It's out of my way.
It's in the opposite direction.

1073
01:40:12,139 --> 01:40:14,232
She doesn't say much.

1074
01:40:14,308 --> 01:40:16,071
I can tell she doesn't want
to talk, so I just...

1075
01:40:16,143 --> 01:40:17,542
leave it.

1076
01:40:23,650 --> 01:40:25,311
But I know this shortcut

1077
01:40:25,386 --> 01:40:28,753
and I just don't...
I just don't think.

1078
01:40:32,626 --> 01:40:35,789
And before I can say,
"This is the short way,"

1079
01:40:35,863 --> 01:40:37,694
she's gone.

1080
01:40:38,966 --> 01:40:40,866
What do you mean,
she's gone?

1081
01:41:03,190 --> 01:41:04,122
Hey!

1082
01:41:05,859 --> 01:41:07,053
Wait!

1083
01:41:28,115 --> 01:41:30,310
-
I'm not going to hurt you.

1084
01:41:31,785 --> 01:41:33,184
Trust me!

1085
01:41:55,976 --> 01:41:57,500
You know...

1086
01:41:59,379 --> 01:42:00,971
I thought that...

1087
01:42:01,982 --> 01:42:04,416
if I'd leave her alone...

1088
01:42:05,686 --> 01:42:07,813
she'd stop
being afraid of me.

1089
01:42:11,792 --> 01:42:13,123
I just...

1090
01:42:15,262 --> 01:42:17,594
I just left her there.

1091
01:42:26,773 --> 01:42:29,207
When I got home,
I saw her...

1092
01:42:31,645 --> 01:42:34,205
I saw her shoe

1093
01:42:34,281 --> 01:42:37,148
on the floor of my car.

1094
01:42:42,256 --> 01:42:43,848
And l...

1095
01:42:48,061 --> 01:42:51,360
Jesus, I just wanted
to help the woman...

1096
01:42:55,102 --> 01:42:57,036
Why didn't you report it, Nik?

1097
01:42:58,739 --> 01:43:01,867
Because I thought
she'd be all right.

1098
01:43:02,943 --> 01:43:05,343
I thought she'd find
her way out of there.

1099
01:43:10,484 --> 01:43:12,042
Then when l...

1100
01:43:14,321 --> 01:43:16,448
and when
I saw her on the news...

1101
01:43:17,591 --> 01:43:20,287
that she was missing, l...

1102
01:43:28,001 --> 01:43:31,459
By then who was going
to believe me?

1103
01:43:44,518 --> 01:43:46,110
Thank you...

1104
01:43:47,187 --> 01:43:48,950
for letting me know.

1105
01:43:50,524 --> 01:43:51,991
Bye.

1106
01:44:18,719 --> 01:44:21,187
Paula? Come in.

1107
01:44:21,255 --> 01:44:22,984
Hi.

1108
01:44:28,328 --> 01:44:30,387
Hey, sweetie.

1109
01:44:33,900 --> 01:44:37,301
- Daddy will be home soon.
- Maybe they can come back later.

1110
01:44:37,371 --> 01:44:41,171
- They've been so good for me.
- No, I don't think so.

1111
01:44:43,176 --> 01:44:44,473
Paula.

1112
01:44:45,646 --> 01:44:47,614
He didn't do it, Jane.

1113
01:44:50,417 --> 01:44:52,112
How do you know?

1114
01:44:55,589 --> 01:44:57,147
He told me.

1115
01:45:04,831 --> 01:45:06,059
Paula?

1116
01:45:07,501 --> 01:45:09,435
-
What could I do, Paula?

1117
01:45:11,204 --> 01:45:12,364
All right.

1118
01:45:12,439 --> 01:45:15,738
Go inside and put
your bags in your rooms.

1119
01:45:30,957 --> 01:45:32,618
Stupid...

1120
01:45:35,162 --> 01:45:37,653
You've got no right, Jane!

1121
01:45:37,731 --> 01:45:39,665
You hear me?!

1122
01:45:39,733 --> 01:45:41,667
You have no fucking right!

1123
01:45:41,735 --> 01:45:45,034
I don't want to see you
anywhere near my kids again.

1124
01:47:39,286 --> 01:47:41,982
I was home, Leon.

1125
01:47:47,394 --> 01:47:49,760
I didn't pick up the phone.

1126
01:47:53,867 --> 01:47:56,301
- John? There's a man...

1127
01:47:56,369 --> 01:47:58,132
Patrick.

1128
01:47:58,205 --> 01:48:00,298
He's a client and he's...

1129
01:48:00,373 --> 01:48:02,204
he's gay.

1130
01:48:04,544 --> 01:48:08,537
I don't understand this.
I don't understand...

1131
01:48:08,615 --> 01:48:09,946
us...

1132
01:48:10,016 --> 01:48:12,143
anymore.

1133
01:48:12,219 --> 01:48:15,882
I don't want this
to be happening to us.

1134
01:48:17,524 --> 01:48:20,493
Oh... there are lights.

1135
01:48:20,560 --> 01:48:23,222
There's a car coming.
I'll wave it down.

1136
01:48:24,865 --> 01:48:28,323
Wait for me.
We'll talk when I get home, okay?

1137
01:48:28,401 --> 01:48:30,096
Bye.

1138
01:48:30,170 --> 01:48:32,400
I love you.

1139
01:48:39,479 --> 01:48:42,607
I thought she would come home.

1140
01:49:39,940 --> 01:49:43,341
- It's not that he might have...

1141
01:49:43,410 --> 01:49:46,004
slept with another woman.

1142
01:49:48,214 --> 01:49:49,476
It's...

1143
01:49:51,117 --> 01:49:53,642
that he might not tell me.

1144
01:49:55,589 --> 01:49:57,819
That would be the betrayal.

1145
01:50:01,761 --> 01:50:03,888
- Do you still love him?

1146
01:50:12,505 --> 01:50:14,803
- Yeah.

1147
01:50:14,874 --> 01:50:16,637
I still love him.

1148
01:52:05,251 --> 01:52:07,776
I don't want to lose you.

1149
01:52:09,889 --> 01:52:11,914
What?

1150
01:52:14,561 --> 01:52:17,428
I don't want to lose you.
I couldn't bear it.
